922c|n|One of a number of narrow strips of wood, or narrow iron plates, placed edge to edge to form the sides, covering, or lining of a vessel or structure; esp., one of the strips which form the sides of a cask, a pail, etc. ; One of the cylindrical bars of a lantern wheel; one of the bars or rounds of a rack, a ladder, etc. ; A metrical portion; a stanza; a staff. ; The five horizontal and parallel lines on and between which musical notes are written or pointed; the staff. ; To break in a stave or the staves of; to break a hole in; to burst; -- often with in; as, to stave a cask; to stave in a boat. ; To push, as with a staff; -- with off. ; To delay by force or craft; to drive away; -- usually with off; as, to stave off the execution of a project. ; To suffer, or cause, to be lost by breaking the cask. ; To furnish with staves or rundles. ; To render impervious or solid by driving with a calking iron; as, to stave lead, or the joints of pipes into which lead has been run.	a:9tvk,111,15;62hq,92,24;3twp,78,12;5eo7,54,38;a5gj,44,10;120p,42,16;5ssn,38,7;9ql5,36,24;9lrd,31,8;34jj,29,8;8pm3,26,17;8egs,11,9;6azn,6,4;88v3,3,15;7h25,1,1~5eo7,54,38;9ql5,36,24;62hq,92,24;8pm3,26,17;120p,42,16;88v3,3,15;9tvk,111,15;3twp,78,12;a5gj,44,10;8egs,11,9;9lrd,31,8;34jj,29,8;5ssn,38,7;6azn,6,4;7h25,1,1	v:2lz6,71,4;1ogb,44,5~1ogb,44,5;2lz6,71,4	V:1vsv,38,3;91cf,22,3;1t6x,18,6;5of1,15,10;8nd4,9,3~5of1,15,10;1t6x,18,6;8nd4,9,3;91cf,22,3;1vsv,38,3	n:6qtt,140,3;1k74,101,9;stc,83,15;12bv,65,3;a5gj,63,37;4n89,48,3;62ho,37,4;120p,18,3;9cwi,14,2;70mg,8,3~a5gj,63,37;stc,83,15;1k74,101,9;62ho,37,4;12bv,65,3;4n89,48,3;120p,18,3;70mg,8,3;6qtt,140,3;9cwi,14,2	N:1icn,57,1;6f7u,36,6;59sw,32,15;1t6x,24,9;6f42,22,2;91cf,16,2;8nd4,3,2~59sw,32,15;1t6x,24,9;6f7u,36,6;8nd4,3,2;6f42,22,2;91cf,16,2;1icn,57,1
