93dg|v|To lay up; to put aside for future use; to store, as merchandise, and the like. ; To provide with material requisites; to store; to fill; to supply; as, to stock a warehouse, that is, to fill it with goods; to stock a farm, that is, to supply it with cattle and tools; to stock land, that is, to occupy it with a permanent growth, especially of grass. ; To suffer to retain milk for twenty-four hours or more previous to sale, as cows. ; To put in the stocks.	o:9n21,29,2;2ysn,14,1;844m,9,16;73q1,4,5;oqr,2,10;9n1z,2,2;507f,1,1~844m,9,16;oqr,2,10;73q1,4,5;9n1z,2,2;9n21,29,2;2ysn,14,1;507f,1,1	s:blb,64,8;m6j,51,14;43b1,16,7~m6j,51,14;blb,64,8;43b1,16,7
