945z|n|Race; stock; generation; descent; family. ; Hereditary character, quality, or disposition. ; Rank; a sort. ; The act of straining, or the state of being strained. ; A violent effort; an excessive and hurtful exertion or tension, as of the muscles; as, he lifted the weight with a strain; the strain upon a ship's rigging in a gale; also, the hurt or injury resulting; a sprain. ; A change of form or dimensions of a solid or liquid mass, produced by a stress. ; A portion of music divided off by a double bar; a complete musical period or sentence; a movement, or any rounded subdivision of a movement. ; Any sustained note or movement; a song; a distinct portion of an ode or other poem; also, the pervading note, or burden, of a song, poem, oration, book, etc.; theme; motive; manner; style; also, a course of action or conduct; as, he spoke in a noble strain; there was a strain of woe in his story; a strain of trickery appears in his career. ; Turn; tendency; inborn disposition. Cf. 1st Strain.	a:74ta,127,8;wog,123,16;5hej,122,5;a26h,121,36;9r4e,118,110;2duj,118,22;92r2,109,101;adbs,107,20;3csm,102,1;a1kz,100,75;6zpm,98,6;2eym,94,1;aejf,94,79;1qc3,94,41;4ggk,94,5~5yo3,15,658;614m,27,575;5776,33,352;4gr,39,259;5okf,69,238;34jj,37,213;a37k,62,211;8li7,90,188;9ra8,31,179;7x9q,87,169;2sug,75,165;9r4e,118,110;6x9o,19,106;92r2,109,101;7h25,28,98	v:5pyj,115,2;1dfd,98,7;9bw6,89,10;8lif,81,12;1dfc,81,1;5xdp,77,10;7vtt,67,12;7vtz,59,2;9hm4,58,2;mot,57,4;v3y,55,21;8li7,53,14;92r2,53,2;9hq5,50,3;aqzj,47,17~82lb,46,180;7k8q,10,114;7hyj,17,98;1bsj,21,82;7toc,31,74;7kcm,25,54;1883,1,48;1bt2,24,41;7kbw,32,40;138x,33,35;4f2a,24,29;4f20,35,28;1bsr,18,25;7tp9,34,23;5ohw,33,21	V:3jn9,110,12;3yzc,83,36;3kyi,79,23;7vtp,75,2;7vtz,69,4;3kyk,66,3;7vtu,64,7;62pg,53,2;3yz9,47,4;7vtt,32,1;4fya,31,17;1bsk,30,58;7frd,28,22;agrv,21,22;1bsr,18,25~1bsk,30,58;3yzc,83,36;u0q,12,28;1bsr,18,25;3kyi,79,23;agrv,21,22;7frd,28,22;1olc,0,22;4fya,31,17;3jn9,110,12;6k5l,4,8;7vtu,64,7;9hqk,5,4;7vtz,69,4;3yz9,47,