958k|n|A line, or long, narrow division of anything of a different color or structure from the ground; hence, any linear variation of color or structure; as, a stripe, or streak, of red on a green ground; a raised stripe. ; A pattern produced by arranging the warp threads in sets of alternating colors, or in sets presenting some other contrast of appearance. ; A strip, or long, narrow piece attached to something of a different color; as, a red or blue stripe sewed upon a garment. ; A stroke or blow made with a whip, rod, scourge, or the like, such as usually leaves a mark. ; A long, narrow discoloration of the skin made by the blow of a lash, rod, or the like. ; Color indicating a party or faction; hence, distinguishing characteristic; sign; likeness; sort; as, persons of the same political stripe. ; The chevron on the coat of a noncommissioned officer.	a:5xng,88,1;5h5t,84,35;5hd6,82,645;at25,68,9;aj94,61,437;ar2j,61,109;abfv,55,123;2eo9,53,71;7k0h,52,18;6us3,52,4;45jk,52,87;ys5,51,257;3udu,49,28;9lm9,47,35;66xv,45,29~5hd6,82,645;aj94,61,437;ys5,51,257;7t8z,44,162;abfv,55,123;3ifa,27,113;ar2j,61,109;zxf,43,92;45jk,52,87;3uj8,43,80;2eo9,53,71;6oym,44,44;8s1h,11,41;ajfk,13,39;9lm9,47,35	v:8r0j,68,1;at25,68,9;5h5t,58,6;4jup,54,46;1nva,44,13;4juh,38,31;1sza,37,4;958k,33,2;4juj,29,11;4dkf,22,14;4j9g,21,19;9ink,15,23;4dk7,15,14;333o,13,24;5hd2,13,1~a7g2,13,445;4jup,54,46;1883,3,33;4juh,38,31;a7cv,4,24;333o,13,24;9ink,15,23;4j9g,21,19;4dkf,22,14;4dk7,15,14;1nva,44,13;4juj,29,11;at25,68,9;5h5t,58,6;1sza,37,4	V:ahk4,91,12;amh7,71,1;6um4,61,22;ahk3,54,2;8qgg,34,19;4fnq,29,19;8gvf,19,10;7i03,17,18;9pso,16,16;ggp,15,29;6ksz,14,4;3sf5,12,28;6yg2,9,4;1ryk,7,19;an5a,5,3~86xk,5,39;ggp,15,29;3sf5,12,28;6um4,61,22;8qgg,34,19;4fnq,29,19;1ryk,7,19;7i03,17,18;9dwt,3,16;9pso,16,16;7yfa,5,13;35j3,4,12;ahk4,91,12;8gvf,19,10;6ksz,14,4	n:958m,129,3;5h5t,105,150;8r0j,98,8;6m7r,96,5;8lc9,93,7;at25,90,43;1arx,81,5;1oz5,78,73;7ov2,72,205;9nay,70,22;6m6e,64,6;2lqi,61,1;958k,55,9;6wq7,54,24;5g5x,5