95gv|n|A metallic element of the calcium group, always naturally occurring combined, as in the minerals strontianite, celestite, etc. It is isolated as a yellowish metal, somewhat malleable but harder than calcium. It is chiefly employed (as in the nitrate) to color pyrotechnic flames red. Symbol Sr. Atomic weight 87.3. ; A radioactive isotope of strontium produced by certain nuclear reactions, and constituting one of the prominent harmful components of radioactive fallout from nuclear explosions; also called radiostrontium. It has a half-life of 28 years.	a:7oj3,94,3;8pm3,22,4~8pm3,22,4;7oj3,94,3	V:7frq,35,1;sbb,22,4~sbb,22,4;7frq,35,1	n:86db,147,8;rx0,139,8;17t3,116,17;8zh7,78,4;7frx,28,4;aj3h,22,8;598y,9,13;w46,2,2~17t3,116,17;598y,9,13;86db,147,8;rx0,139,8;aj3h,22,8;8zh7,78,4;7frx,28,4;w46,2,2	N:b6o,181,16;9ol3,173,10;asbs,147,3;1i1e,146,4;rx0,143,11;4oug,118,5;4mcq,117,3;488i,116,9;6cju,114,5;1hd4,112,11;98p5,110,4;19zq,110,5;4ouc,101,4;4mfb,87,6;4mgj,83,4~b6o,181,16;rx0,143,11;1hd4,112,11;9ol3,173,10;488i,116,9;4mfb,87,6;6cju,114,5;4oug,118,5;19zq,110,5;1i1e,146,4;4ouc,101,4;4mgj,83,4;98p5,110,4;2kt7,57,3;8zh7,74,3
